            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent abdominal pain in school children: the loneliness of the long-distance physician.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>969-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The recurring of abdominal pain can be a taxing clinical ordeal for the primary care physician or consultant. It often is a test of stamina, of diagnostic self-confidence, of fiscal constraint, and of vigilance for rare conditions. The clinician is apt to be haunted by the lingering question: &quot;Am I missing something?&quot; That which might or might not be &quot;missed&quot; comprises the content as well as the rationale for this review.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
